        "geology": "The geology at this site is characteristic of schist, migmatite, and biotitic gneiss.",
        "hydrology": "Snowmelt dominates the hydrologic and nutrient flux in this 4.9 km2 (1211 acre) watershed. Peak streamflow occurs in the summer (June) of each year and sharply declines throughout late summer. Discharge remains very low through the winter months. While weather systems from across the continental divide are the most common source of precipitation, spring and early summer thunderstorms can also contribute to the flow of the creek.",
